only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a379bd67-5a45-55a8-a720-5261bcae893e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359284} {:answer/id #uuid "7026c0d8-9d58-5956-9a5d-f88e02d76090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359285} {:answer/id #uuid "5d402865-d2d4-5b11-899f-8790598fd3ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359286} {:answer/id #uuid "74cdfe0d-5f29-5e27-bb71-3da207682e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359287} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa3ecd5-ecbf-5d38-99b4-886eaf945077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a379bd67-5a45-55a8-a720-5261bcae893e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359284} :answer-field/id #uuid "60a73d3c-fbad-50b9-8edb-6789b179afbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359283}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be636e7b-176b-576c-ba50-fdd7d8a98ef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161642" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}\\le 1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x-{x}^{2}}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96030885-a8fe-5380-a4eb-46d203537722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359291} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c08b1b-0853-596f-adc6-2f414b9a22a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359292} {:answer